Also note the **already-passing pattern for "not available" errors** in `CGR Rental Tests.CheckOutTwiceFails` / `SuspendRentalsBlocksCheckout` — both assert `Assert.ExpectedError('Vehicle <No> is not available.')`, i.e., the existing `NotAvailableErr` label in `CGR Rental Mgt`. A due-for-service checkout block would naturally produce the same error message if it's wired through `IsAvailable`.

